#18601
The Hall of First Steps~
Polished flagstones form a simple instructional hall just inside the Academia. Brass direction markers have been set into the floor, and a large compass rose fills the center of the chamber. Benches along the walls give new arrivals a place to collect themselves before proceeding. The lesson here is deliberately simple: learn to observe the room, notice its exits, and move with purpose.
~
