#18610
The Hall of Recovery~
Low cots, water basins, folded blankets, and simple wooden screens make this a calm place for students to recover after drills. Instructors use the room to teach the value of REST, SLEEP, WAKE, STAND, and watching health, mana, and movement before continuing. The atmosphere is intentionally peaceful, a reminder that surviving an adventure includes knowing when to stop.
~
