#18620
Entrance to the Examination Grounds~
The polished stone of the Academia gives way to older masonry here, deliberately preserved as part of the practical course. A bronze plaque announces the Examination Grounds and reminds students that the lessons beyond are less guided. The passages ahead are meant to test observation, navigation, judgment, and combat under controlled but believable conditions.
~
